{"name":"Lime Lightning","hex":"#befd73","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lime","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any inorganic material containing calcium, usually calcium oxide (quicklime) or calcium hydroxide (slaked lime).","Any gluey or adhesive substance that traps or captures; sometimes a synonym for birdlime."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To treat with calcium hydroxide or calcium oxide (lime).","To smear with birdlime.\n To ensnare, catch, entrap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lime"},{"term":"lightning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flash of light produced by short-duration, high-voltage discharge of electricity within a cloud, between clouds, or between a cloud and the earth.","A discharge of this kind."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extremely fast or sudden; moving (as if) at the speed of lightning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lightning"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lightning","blocks":[{"text":"Lightning is a natural phenomenon consisting of electrostatic discharges occurring through the atmosphere between two electrically charged regions. One or both regions are within the atmosphere, with the second region sometimes occurring on the ground. Following the lightning, the regions become partially or wholly electrically neutralized."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg/330px-Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lightning","wikidata":"Q33741"},{"title":"Lime (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lime is a color that is a shade of yellow-green, so named because it is a representation of the color of the citrus fruit lime. It is the color that is in between the web color chartreuse and yellow on the color wheel. Alternate names for this color included yellow-green, lemon-lime, lime green, or bitter lime."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg/330px-AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(color)","wikidata":"Q906936"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Earth_cutaway.png/500px-Earth_cutaway.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Earth_cutaway.png/500px-Earth_cutaway.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEarth_cutaway.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Anvil-to-ground_lightning.jpg/500px-Anvil-to-ground_lightning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Anvil-to-ground_lightning.jpg/500px-Anvil-to-ground_lightning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A bolt from the blue lightning strike which appears to initiate from a clear patch of sky, but the turbulent sky above the anvil cloud drives a bolt of plasma through the cloud directly to the ground. They are commonly referred to as positive flashes, despite the fact that they are usually negative in polarity.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnvil-to-ground_lightning.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Ligtning_new_delhi_view_1.GIF/330px-Ligtning_new_delhi_view_1.GIF?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f4/Ligtning_new_delhi_view_1.GIF?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"